  "id": "direct-reflex",
  "term": "direct reflex",
  "definition": "A direct reflex is a reflex pathway in the spinal cord in which an incoming sensory fibre sends a collateral directly to cells in the ventral horn, forming a direct reflex arc to a motor neuron. In this historical usage, it is contrasted with an indirect reflex path that passes through an intercalary cell.",
